    pr_ref:  # bd8e
    description: "WHAT (proposed by the reviewer; the owner was receptive in session)\nOne fixture, written once per language, that pins the same call shapes everywhere: two classes that both declare execute(), a factory get_db() returning one of them, and\n  db = get_db(); db.execute()      get_db().execute()      c = Conn(); c.execute()\nplus an inherited method, an ambiguous name that must stay unresolved, and an imported callee. The reviewer's table on 10.0.0: Java, Python, Swift resolve all three; C#, Go, Kotlin, TypeScript leave the chain unresolved; Rust binds two of three to the wrong class at 0.85.\nRe-run on dev fc8c8cb19 by the filing agent: the Rust and TypeScript rows only (fixtures ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/outside_review_11242026/fx/rs, fx/tsx; items filed the same day for each).\n\nWHY\nThe same three ideas give three behaviours across eight analyzers; ADR-0029 already replaced per-language copies of inherited-call resolution with one shared linker, and variable/return typing (ADR-0006) and imports (ADR-0007) stayed per-language. The fixture shows divergence without deciding anything; whether to build a shared resolver is a separate decision for the owner and is NOT asked here.\n\nREPORTED, NOT RE-RUN. Source: an outside reviewer who tried hypergumbo 10.0.0 from PyPI on 2026-11-24 (transcript pasted by the owner in session). Nothing in this item was run on dev by the filing agent unless a line says so; the reviewer's fixtures are not on this machine. FIRST STEP: reproduce on current dev with a fixture, and check the unreleased changelog, before building anything. Filed at the owner's request (\"file them all now\")."  # bd8e
    fields: {}  # bd8e
